     6	// Unicode decimal digit as its ASCII counterpart. Only then does the ASCII
     7	// scanner run, and that scanner accepts a narrower whitespace set. This is why
     8	// '١٠', '１０' and '\xa010' all parse while '\x1c10' and '﻿10' do not.
